---
/**
 * Montecito, CA — estate-belt city pillar (feat/santa-barbara Stage B).
 * Branch: Santa Barbara — service_area (no public street address).
 *
 * Angle (distinct from /santa-barbara/): the estate belt. Aging built-in
 * Sub-Zero installs (500-series from late-'80s/'90s kitchens, 600-series from
 * the 2000s) that have outlived their original service relationships, Wolf
 * ranges, Viking outdoor kitchens, wine rooms — and the property managers and
 * estate managers who are the actual callers on most Montecito jobs.
 *
 * Zero-invention notes:
 *   - Sub-Zero series framing matches our own
 *     /services/refrigerator-repair/sub-zero-problems-by-series/ page (500/600
 *     series eras, evaporator/defrost wear patterns). No invented model digits.
 *   - No ReviewsBlock — no verifiable Montecito reviews yet, inventing quotes
 *     is prohibited.
 *   - Residential page → $89 only, no $120.
 *   - Schema: single LocalBusiness for the SB branch, NO location array.
 */

import CityLayoutV2 from '../layouts/CityLayoutV2.astro';
import HeroSection from '../components/cities/v2/HeroSection.astro';
import TrustBadgesRow from '../components/cities/v2/TrustBadgesRow.astro';
import IntroNarrative from '../components/cities/v2/IntroNarrative.astro';
import ServicesGrid from '../components/cities/v2/ServicesGrid.astro';
import CustomNarrative from '../components/cities/v2/CustomNarrative.astro';
import ServiceArea from '../components/cities/v2/ServiceArea.astro';
import RecentRepairs from '../components/cities/v2/RecentRepairs.astro';
import WhyCallsUsBack from '../components/cities/v2/WhyCallsUsBack.astro';
import PricingCards from '../components/cities/v2/PricingCards.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../components/cities/v2/FAQAccordion.astro';
import AlsoServingNearby from '../components/cities/v2/AlsoServingNearby.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../components/cities/v2/FinalCTA.astro';
import { CITIES } from '../data/cities';
import { BRANCHES } from '../data/branches';
import { OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA } from '../data/business-hours';
import { mergeCredentials } from '../data/credentials-schema';

const citySlug = 'montecito';
const city = CITIES.find((c) => c.slug === citySlug)!;
const branch = BRANCHES.find((b) => b.slug === city.primaryBranch)!;

const cityName = 'Montecito';
const zips = ['93108'];

const phoneRaw = `+1${branch.phone.replace(/\D/g, '')}`;

const title = `Appliance Repair Montecito CA — Same Day Service`;
const description = "Same-day appliance repair in Montecito 93108 — aging Sub-Zero built-ins, Wolf ranges, outdoor kitchens, wine rooms. Estate managers welcome. (805) 500-0855.";
const canonical = 'https://samedayappliance.repair/montecito/';

const localBusinessSchema = mergeCredentials({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HomeAndConstructionBusiness',
  name: branch.fullName,
  image: 'https://samedayappliance.repair/images/logo.webp',
  url: canonical,
  telephone: phoneRaw,
  email: branch.email,
  areaServed: [
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Montecito', sameAs: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montecito,_California' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Upper Village' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Lower Village' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Coast Village Road' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Butterfly Beach' }
  ],
  openingHoursSpecification: OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA,
  priceRange: '$$$',
  license: 'BHGS #A49573'
});

const introParagraphs = [
  "<strong>When an appliance fails in Montecito, our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair usually find one of the same few stories: a built-in Sub-Zero from a '90s or 2000s kitchen remodel that has outlived its original service relationship and is now running on tired defrost components and a struggling evaporator fan, a Wolf range that needs an igniter and a calibration rather than a replacement, a Viking outdoor kitchen with salt-corroded igniters, or a wine room drifting warm. We dispatch same-day across the Upper Village, Lower Village, and the Coast Village Road corridor. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), BBB Accredited.</strong>",
  "Montecito kitchens have a particular history. A large share of the estate housing here was built or remodeled in the late '80s through the 2000s, and the built-in refrigeration that went in then — Sub-Zero 500-series in the earlier kitchens, 600-series in the later ones — is still in the walls. These units were built to be serviced for decades, and they reward proper service. The problem is that many of them haven't had any: the original installer retired, the service company that knew the unit folded, and the estate has been running on crossed fingers since. We service these series with OEM parts, and our <a href=\"/services/refrigerator-repair/sub-zero-problems-by-series/\">Sub-Zero problems-by-series guide</a> explains what each generation typically needs.",
  "The other thing we know about Montecito: the person calling us is often not the person who owns the appliance. Estate managers, property managers, house managers, personal assistants — most of our Montecito calls are placed by professionals managing the property on the owner's behalf. We work that way comfortably: written estimates that can be forwarded for approval, scheduling around household calendars, invoicing to the management office, and discretion as a default, not a special request.",
  `Diagnostic fee: <strong>$89</strong> — waived with repair. Written estimate before we start. <strong>90-day warranty</strong> on parts and labor. Call <a href="tel:${phoneRaw}">${branch.phone}</a> for same-day service across 93108 — and the rest of the <a href="/santa-barbara-county/">South Coast corridor</a>.`,
  "<strong>From our techs on Montecito refrigeration:</strong> if your built-in Sub-Zero is more than fifteen years old and nobody has serviced it in the last three, have the condenser cleaned and the defrost system checked before it fails on its own schedule. These units almost always warn you — longer run times, a warmer top shelf, frost where there wasn't frost — and the cheap visit is the one you book before the food is at risk."
];

const services = [
  { icon: '🧊', name: 'Built-In Refrigeration', slug: 'refrigerator', issues: 'Aging Sub-Zero 500/600-series · Defrost wear · Evaporator fans · Door seals', brands: 'Sub-Zero · GE Monogram · Thermador · Viking · Miele' },
  { icon: '🍷', name: 'Wine Cellar Cooling', slug: 'wine-cellar', issues: 'Wine room cooling · Temperature drift · Humidity · Cellar conversions', brands: 'Sub-Zero · EuroCave · Liebherr · U-Line · WhisperKool' },
  { icon: '🔥', name: 'Range & Oven Repair', slug: 'oven', issues: 'Igniters · Calibration · Dual-fuel · Steam ovens', brands: 'Wolf · Viking · Thermador · Miele · Lacanche · La Cornue' },
  { icon: '🔆', name: 'Outdoor Kitchen Repair', slug: 'bbq', issues: 'Grill igniters · Burners · Outdoor refrigeration · Side burners', brands: 'Viking · Lynx · Fire Magic · Twin Eagles · DCS · Wolf' },
  { icon: '🍽️', name: 'Dishwasher Repair', slug: 'dishwasher', issues: 'Panel-front units · Hard-water scale · Leak codes', brands: 'Miele · Bosch · Thermador · KitchenAid' },
  { icon: '🫧', name: 'Washer & Dryer Repair', slug: 'washer', issues: 'Laundry rooms · Stacked units · Scale buildup', brands: 'Miele · LG · Speed Queen · Whirlpool · Samsung' },
  { icon: '❄️', name: 'Freezer & Undercounter', slug: 'freezer', issues: 'Sub-Zero columns · Undercounter drawers · Ice makers', brands: 'Sub-Zero · U-Line · True · Perlick' },
  { icon: '♨️', name: 'Cooktop Repair', slug: 'cooktop', issues: "Burners won't light · Induction · Downdraft", brands: 'Wolf · Viking · Thermador · Miele · Gaggenau' }
];

const estateNarrative = {
  eyebrow: 'THE AGING BUILT-IN PROBLEM',
  headline: 'Montecito Has Decades of Built-In Refrigeration Nobody Has Been Servicing',
  paragraphs: [
    "Walk into a Montecito kitchen and there's a decent chance the built-in refrigerator predates the smartphone. Sub-Zero 500-series units went into estate kitchens here through the late '80s and '90s; the 600-series followed through the 2000s. These machines were engineered for long service lives — which is exactly why so many are still running — but 'built to last' was never 'built to be ignored.' Compressors, defrost components, evaporator fans, and door gaskets all have wear schedules, and a unit that has run twenty years without attention is running on borrowed time.",
    "The service history gap is the real Montecito pattern. The company that installed the unit is gone. The one technician who knew it retired. The estate changed hands and the binder with the service records didn't survive the move. So the first time anyone calls us about a given kitchen, we're often the first technician to open that unit in a decade. That's fine — it's what we're for. We diagnose the unit as it actually is, tell you honestly what's worth doing, and leave you with a written record so the next fifteen years aren't a mystery too.",
    "And when a unit genuinely is at the end — a sealed-system failure on a thirty-year-old 500-series, say — we say that plainly and help you think through the replacement rather than selling you a repair that won't hold. Repair-versus-replace honesty is policy here, not a slogan."
  ]
};

const estateManagerNarrative = {
  eyebrow: 'ESTATE MANAGERS & PROPERTY MANAGERS',
  headline: 'Built for How Montecito Households Actually Run',
  paragraphs: [
    "On most Montecito calls, our point of contact is an estate manager, house manager, or property management office — not the owner. That changes how service needs to work, and we've shaped our process around it.",
    "Written estimates go out promptly so they can be forwarded for approval without a second site visit. We schedule around household calendars — deliveries, events, the hours when service traffic is welcome and the hours when it isn't. Invoices go to the management office, itemized the way bookkeepers want them. Gate codes and access notes stay in the job record so the second visit doesn't repeat the first visit's logistics. And discretion is the default: unmarked interactions with neighbors, no photographs beyond what the work requires, no commentary about whose kitchen we were in.",
    "If you manage more than one property on the South Coast, one number covers all of them — Montecito, <a href=\"/santa-barbara/\">Santa Barbara</a>, Hope Ranch, Summerland, Carpinteria, and Goleta run from the same branch, with the same techs and the same paper trail."
  ]
};

const neighborhoods = [
  { name: 'Upper Village', zip: '93108', featured: true },
  { name: 'Lower Village', zip: '93108', featured: true },
  { name: 'Coast Village Road corridor', zip: '93108', featured: true },
  { name: 'Butterfly Beach area', zip: '93108' },
  { name: 'Hedgerow district', zip: '93108' },
  { name: 'Cold Spring area', zip: '93108' },
